# RSF01-01: whose X-Forwarded-For is believed.
title X-Forwarded-For is believed only from a trusted proxy; from anyone else it is removed, and the direct address counts
row  lb:box "Your load balancer" "a trusted proxy" | shield:warnbox "request-shield" "reads right to left" | client:okbox "The visitor's address" "its bucket: IPv4, IPv6 /64"
row  other:box "Anyone else" "X-Forwarded-For: made up" | stripped:nobox "Headers removed" "the direct address counts"
arrow lb -> shield "X-Forwarded-For"
arrow shield -> client "believed" go
arrow other -> stripped "not trusted"
note The application sees the same address, scheme and host as the shield.
